[[:db/cas 17592186058071 :answer/value "$$7889$" "$\\$7889$"] [:db/cas 17592186058072 :answer/value "$$7783$" "$\\$7783$"] [:db/cas 17592186058073 :answer/value "$$7852$" "$\\$7852$"] [:db/cas 17592186058074 :answer/value "$$7900$" "$\\$7900$"] [:db/cas 17592186058075 :answer/value "$$7921$" "$\\$7921$"] [:db/cas 17592186058957 :answer/value "$$3.37$ per gallon" "$\\$3.37$ per gallon"] [:db/cas 17592186058958 :answer/value "$$3.05$ per gallon" "$\\$3.05$ per gallon"] [:db/cas 17592186058959 :answer/value "$$3.27$ per gallon" "$\\$3.27$ per gallon"] [:db/cas 17592186058960 :answer/value "$$3.43$ per gallon" "$\\$3.43$ per gallon"] [:db/cas 17592186058961 :answer/value "$$3.19$ per gallon" "$\\$3.19$ per gallon"] [:db/cas 17592186059595 :question/worked-solution "The continuously compounded growth equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} P &= P_0e^{rt}. \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have a final amount of $P=20\\,500$, a rate of $r=0.052$, and a time duration of $t=14$ days. Substituting these values into the formula and solving for $P_0$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_{0}e^{rt} \\\\\n20500 &= P_{0}e^{(0.052)(14)} \\\\\n20500 &= P_{0}e^{0.728} \\\\\n20500 &= P_{0}(2.07093...) \\\\\nP_{0} &= \\frac{20500}{2.07093...} \\\\\n&= P_{0} \\mid \\approx 9899\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there were $9\\,899$ bacteria initially." "The continuously compounded growth equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} P &= P_0e^{rt}. \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have a final amount of $P=20\\,500$, a rate of $r=0.052$, and a time duration of $t=14$ days. Substituting these values into the formula and solving for $P_0$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_{0}e^{rt} \\\\\n20500 &= P_{0}e^{(0.052)(14)} \\\\\n20500 &= P_{0}e^{0.728} \\\\\n20500 &= P_{0}(2.07093...) \\\\\nP_{0} &= \\frac{20500}{2.07093...} \\\\\nP_{0} &\\approx 9899\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there were $9\\,899$ bacteria initially."] [:db/cas 17592186060056 :question/worked-solution nil "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. Here $P_0=102$, $P=10$, and $r=-0.095$ per year. Solve for $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n10 &= 102e^{-0.095t} \\\\\ne^{-0.095t} &= \\frac{10}{102} \\\\\n-0.095t &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{10}{102}\\right) \\\\\nt &= \\frac{\\ln(10/102)}{-0.095} \\\\\n&\\approx 24.4462.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer gives $24$ years."] [:db/cas 17592186056694 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186056697] [:db/ensure 17592186056694 :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186056697 :answer/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186060056 :question/validate] [:db/cas 17592186060057 :question/worked-solution nil "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. Here $P_0=10$, $P=781$, and $t=14$ minutes. Solve for $r$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n781 &= 10e^{14r} \\\\\ne^{14r} &= \\frac{781}{10} \\\\\n14r &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{781}{10}\\right) \\\\\nr &= \\frac{\\ln(781/10)}{14} \\\\\n&\\approx 0.311285.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe percentage rate is approximately $31.1285\\%$ per minute. Rounding to the nearest percent gives $31\\%$ per minute."] [:db/cas 17592186056700 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186056701] [:db/ensure 17592186056700 :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186056701 :answer/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186060057 :question/validate] [:db/cas 17592186060058 :question/worked-solution nil "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. Here $P_0=4120$, $r=-0.0381$ per year, and $t=2016-2009=7$ years. Substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= 4120e^{(-0.0381)(7)} \\\\\n&= 4120e^{-0.2667} \\\\\n&\\approx 3155.5196.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer gives approximately $3156$ crimes in $2016$."] [:db/cas 17592186056706 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186056711] [:db/ensure 17592186056706 :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186056711 :answer/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186060058 :question/validate] [:db/cas 17592186060059 :question/worked-solution nil "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. Here $P_0=9830$ and $r=-0.18$ per day. Convert $2$ weeks to $t=14$ days, then substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= 9830e^{(-0.18)(14)} \\\\\n&= 9830e^{-2.52} \\\\\n&\\approx 790.9179.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer gives approximately $791$ people."] [:db/cas 17592186056712 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186056715] [:db/ensure 17592186056712 :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186056715 :answer/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186060059 :question/validate] [:db/cas 17592186060238 :question/worked-solution nil "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. Here $P=16700$, $r=0.15$ per year, and $t=5$ years. Solve for the earlier profit $P_0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n16700 &= P_0e^{(0.15)(5)} \\\\\nP_0 &= \\frac{16700}{e^{0.75}} \\\\\n&\\approx 7888.5214.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest dollar, the profit five years ago was $\\$7889$."] [:db/cas 17592186058070 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186058071] [:db/ensure 17592186058070 :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186058071 :answer/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186060238 :question/validate] [:db/cas 17592186060389 :question/worked-solution nil "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. Here $P=3.11$, $r=-0.01$ per month, and $t=5$ months. Solve for the earlier gas price $P_0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3.11 &= P_0e^{(-0.01)(5)} \\\\\nP_0 &= \\frac{3.11}{e^{-0.05}} \\\\\n&\\approx 3.269453.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest cent, the earlier price was $\\$3.27$ per gallon."] [:db/cas 17592186058956 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186058959] [:db/ensure 17592186058956 :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186058959 :answer/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186060389 :question/validate]]
